<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bantĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βαντία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Apulia</i>,
				<i>in the vicinity of Venusia</i>, <i>on the southern declivity of the mountain</i>, now <i>Banzi</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27,
				25, 13</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bantīnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Bantia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 4, 15</span></i>
			.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bantīni</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Bantia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				15, § 98</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
